.TH HD-FONTS 7 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-fonts \- the JetBrains Mono Nerd Font of hyprdebian
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-desktop
holds the font of hyprdebian: JetBrains Mono, the typeface by JetBrains, with
the icons of Nerd Fonts patched in, from the Nerd Fonts release v3.4.0.
They are only the fonts; they have no commands and no settings.
They have no emoji; fontconfig takes those from Noto Color Emoji, of
.BR fonts-noto-color-emoji ,
which
.B hd-desktop
depends on.
.PP
It holds two families, each in 16 styles:
.TP
.B JetBrainsMono Nerd Font
The icons are about one and a half letters wide.
They are easier to see, but can overlap the next letter.
.TP
.B JetBrainsMono Nerd Font Mono
The icons are one letter wide, so every character takes the same width.
Use it where the text has to line up, as in terminals.
.PP
The styles are Thin, ExtraLight, Light, Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold and
ExtraBold, each also in Italic.
Both families keep the ligatures of JetBrains Mono.
.PP
The fonts are in
.IR /usr/share/fonts/truetype/jetbrains-mono-nerd .
fontconfig finds them there, and refreshes its cache when the package is
installed, upgraded or removed.
.SH USING THE FONTS
Name the font in the configuration of a program by a family name, with the
size where it takes one.
The families also have the short names
.B JetBrainsMono NF
and
.BR "JetBrainsMono NFM" ,
and every style but Regular and Bold has a family name of its own, such as
.BR "JetBrainsMono NFM Medium" .
Such a name works in every program: in those that look up a family name,
and in those that read a style after the family, as GTK and Pango do.
HyprDebian uses
.B JetBrainsMono NFM Medium
everywhere.
For example, in
.IR ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf :
.PP
.RS
.nf
font_family JetBrainsMono NFM Medium
.fi
.RE
.PP
or, in a GTK font name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
JetBrainsMono NFM Medium 11
.fi
.RE
.PP
To list the installed styles:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fc\-list : family style | grep \-i 'jetbrainsmono nerd'
.fi
.RE
.PP
A program that draws text from a font file instead of through fontconfig
takes a file from
.IR /usr/share/fonts/truetype/jetbrains-mono-nerd ,
such as
.IR JetBrainsMonoNerdFontMono\-Regular.ttf .
.SH CREDITS
The fonts are the work of others; hd-desktop only installs them, unchanged.
.TP
.B JetBrains Mono
The typeface, made by The JetBrains Mono Project Authors at JetBrains.
.br
https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
.TP
.B Nerd Fonts
The icons and the patched fonts, by Ryan L McIntyre and the Nerd Fonts
contributors.
The icons themselves come from projects such as Font Awesome, Material Design
Icons, Codicons, Devicons, Octicons and Powerline.
.br
https://www.nerdfonts.com/
.SH COPYRIGHT
The fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, as is JetBrains Mono, which
they are derived from.
The icons are under the licenses of their projects.
See
.I /usr/share/doc/hd-desktop/copyright
for the copyright holders and every license, and
.I /usr/share/doc/hd-desktop/nerd\-fonts/OFL.txt
for the license file of the release.
.SH FILES
